  "goodToKnow": "Der Dolch is a dagger. In German history, die Dolchstoßlegende (stab-in-the-back myth) falsely claimed that the undefeated army had been betrayed by socialists and Jews at home in 1918; the Nazis exploited it to undermine the Weimar Republic. Der Dolchstoß is a stab in the back, betrayal. Schiller's ballad Die Bürgschaft begins with a man carrying a dagger. Plural: die Dolche."
